==Battleground==
*25 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
*7 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*5 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*6 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*1 [[Doge]] spawns after 96.67 seconds<sup>2,900f</sup>.
*1 [[Assassin Bear]] spawns after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
If you don't clear the stage within 100 seconds, the 5000% Assassin Bear will result in certain defeat.

Bring along [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] to deal with the Relic Doges and Sir Rels, [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] to deal with the Celeboodles (Money Up [[Talents]] recommended), and [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] to deal with the Doge Darks. Spawn [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] too along with meatshields so as to quicken the process. Also, [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] is a good unit to get rid of the peons, especially at a high level.

==Trivia==
*Shinobi Showdown's Japanese name, Shinobi Ai (忍び遭い, "Shinobi Encounter"), shares its pronunciation with the term 忍び逢い, meaning a secret meeting or rendezvous, such as between lovers, away from the eyes of other people. The only difference is that the stage spells ''Ai'' (逢い, "encounter" or "meeting") as 遭い, which tends to carry a more negative nuance; notably, these terms also sound the same as 愛, meaning love.
**It's possible that the stage's name was mistranslated, as while ''shinobi'' (忍び) exclusively refers to a male ninja in English, it can also mean general stealth or incognito travelling in Japanese.
***This may hint at how the stage contains [[Assassin Bear]] and [[Doge Dark]], as assassins are expected to be stealthy.
*From this point on, all [[Uncanny Legends]] stages contain at least one [[Relic Enemies|Relic]].

